        "original_id": "6405488c-8c98-5f9b-8ad7-6e2ad9522a6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Manettia, Fragaria\n- People: Saverio Manetti, Giovanni Targioni Tozzetti, Carolus Linnaeus\n- Organizations: Orto Botanico di Firenze\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, botanical naming\n\nFacts:\n- Giovanni Targioni Tozzetti was supervisor of the Orto Botanico di Firenze in Florence before Saverio Manetti succeeded him.\n- Carolus Linnaeus named the plant genus Manettia in honour of Saverio Manetti.\n- Manettia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rubiaceae.\n- Fragaria is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rosaceae.\n- Fragaria plants are commonly known as strawberries for their edible fruits.",
